<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>ScreenX — third-party licences</title>
<style>
body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 50rem; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; line-height: 1.5; }
h3 { margin-top: 2.5rem; border-top: 1px solid #ccc; padding-top: 1.5rem; }
ul { padding-left: 1.25rem; }
.license-used-by { columns: 3; font-size: 0.85rem; }
.license-text { white-space: pre-wrap; font-size: 0.8rem; background: #f6f6f6; padding: 1rem; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Third-party licences</h1>

<p>ScreenX is one static binary, so the libraries below are compiled into it.
Each is listed under the licence it is used on, with the full text of that
licence. ScreenX itself is under the GNU General Public License version 3; these
libraries are not, and keep their own terms.</p>

<p>The fonts are the notable case: Ubuntu Light is under the Ubuntu Font Licence,
Noto Emoji under the SIL Open Font Licence. Both allow embedding, and neither
allows release under another licence, so both stay under their own.</p>

<h2>Licences used</h2>
<ul>
{{#each overview}}
    <li><a href="#{{id}}">{{name}}</a> — {{count}}</li>
{{/each}}
</ul>

<h2>Full text</h2>
{{#each licenses}}
<h3 id="{{id}}">{{name}}</h3>
<h4>Used by</h4>
<ul class="license-used-by">
{{#each used_by}}
    <li><a href="{{#if crate.repository}}{{crate.repository}}{{else}}https://crates.io/crates/{{crate.name}}{{/if}}">{{crate.name}} {{crate.version}}</a></li>
{{/each}}
</ul>
<pre class="license-text">{{text}}</pre>
{{/each}}
</body>
</html>
